---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import { dots } from '../lib/patterns.js';
const bodyBg = dots();
import site from '../data/site.json';
const mailto = `mailto:${site.email}?subject=${encodeURIComponent('Project inquiry')}`;
---
<Base title="About" description="JT Embry, owner of Embry Development, LLC in Louisville: ten years of finance and healthcare engineering, now a one-person studio. One email starts a project.">
  <Hero variant="graph" seed={23} diagram="index" eyebrow="About" title="One engineer. No account managers.">
    <p class="lede">When you email {site.legalName}, the person who answers is the person who does the work.</p>
  </Hero>

  <section class="section band-parallax">
    <div class="band-bg" set:html={bodyBg} aria-hidden="true" />
    <div class="wrap">
      <p>I'm JT Embry. For ten years I have built finance and healthcare software, first as an engineer and then as a lead: a SaaS product from an empty repo, a video portal for hospitals, a whole platform moved to a new cloud, and most recently the AI tooling that raised one team's output by 65%.</p>
      <p>Before that I ran a bank's help desk, cleaned LiDAR data for a self-driving program, and studied English literature. The pattern holds: find what slows people down, remove it, and leave them able to do the work without me. I measure a job by how much of it still runs after I have left.</p>
      <p>I formed {site.legalName} in 2026 to do that work for clients: software and AI systems for teams and small practices, sites and automation for small businesses, and, since I put a 3D printer in the shop, physical parts.</p>
      <p>I live in Louisville. Away from the desk, I restore a Ducati Scrambler, train a dog, and read theology.</p>

      <h2 id="contact">One email starts it</h2>
      <p>Tell me the problem in a few sentences. I read everything and reply within two business days, usually sooner.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Software or AI:</strong> what your team or practice wants to do, what blocks it, and any deadline.</li>
        <li><strong>Custom software:</strong> what the business runs on now, where it hurts, and who would log in.</li>
        <li><strong>3D printing:</strong> a photo with something for scale, rough dimensions, how many, and where the part will be used, or the STL file alone.</li>
      </ul>
      <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={mailto}>Email {site.email}</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
